From: xdplus port <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: report 6 GHz band unsupported (MT6630 has no 6E radio)

WifiManager.is6GHzBandSupported() -> WifiServiceImpl.is6GhzBandSupportedInternal()
-> ClientModeImpl.isWifiBandSupported(WIFI_BAND_6_GHZ). The overlay bool
config_wifi6ghzSupport only short-circuits to *true*; when false (default) the
method falls through to mWifiNative.getChannelsForBand(6GHZ).length > 0. The
device's Wi-Fi chip is an MT6630 (2.4/5 GHz 802.11ac) with no 6 GHz radio, but
the legacy MTK Wi-Fi HAL answers the 6 GHz channel query with phantom channels,
so the probe returns true and device-info apps (Athena) wrongly show 6 GHz
"Yes". The resource is true-only so no overlay can force it false; force false
in code for this device. 5 GHz stays on the normal capability path.

See docs/PORTING_LOG.md (2026-07-13 Wi-Fi/Athena triage).
---
diff --git a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
index 14866c8..31d047f 100644
--- a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
+++ b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/ClientModeImpl.java
@@ -1344,10 +1344,12 @@ public class ClientModeImpl extends StateMachine {
         }
 
         if (band == WifiScanner.WIFI_BAND_6_GHZ) {
-            if (mContext.getResources().getBoolean(R.bool.config_wifi6ghzSupport)) {
-                return true;
-            }
-            return (mWifiNative.getChannelsForBand(WifiScanner.WIFI_BAND_6_GHZ).length > 0);
+            // MT6630 has no 6 GHz (Wi-Fi 6E) radio. config_wifi6ghzSupport only
+            // short-circuits to true; keeping the original body would fall through
+            // to the capability probe, and the legacy MTK HAL's
+            // getChannelsForBand(6GHZ) returns phantom channels -> Athena/Settings
+            // wrongly report 6 GHz "Yes". Force false (PORTING_LOG wifi triage).
+            return false;
         }
 
         return false;
